From 6eff3b3adc2f7e33ea302dda37d8b0eaf49d7f25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Belfry <belfry@belfry.local>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:18:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] feat(belfry): e-mail from the ID token; the participant's
 pass on the dashboard

Preloaded accounts have no e-mail, so the dashboard asked them to verify
"()" and the UCAN carried an empty address. On OIDC login the ID token's
`email` is now stored on the account as verified (OIDC_TRUST_EMAIL, default
true): the provider only lets a participant in through a magic link to that
address. An address held by another account of the tenant is left alone.

GET /api/user/pass (session auth) reads the pass behind the account's
vine_id (`odoo-partner-<id>`) from the onboarding service
(BELFRY_PASS_INFO_URL + PASS_INFO_TOKEN, `GET /admin/partners/<id>/pass`)
and the dashboard shows a "Your pass" card: tier, validity, state, member
number and "Add to your wallet" (the claim link) while the pass is active
and unclaimed. 404 without a pass, 503 when the service is not configured;
the card is hidden in both cases.
